# Store and check out every file byte for byte.
#
# This is not a style preference. Several projects prove a claim by regenerating a
# document and comparing its SHA-256 against the copy committed here -- that is what
# makes "this report was produced by running the code" checkable rather than assertable.
#
# With Git's default end-of-line conversion on Windows (core.autocrlf=true), cloning
# rewrites every LF in those committed reports to CRLF, while the generator that
# rebuilds them still writes LF. The hashes then differ for a reason that has nothing
# to do with the code, and the failure lands on whoever cloned the repository rather
# than on whoever introduced it.
#
# `-text` disables the conversion in both directions, for everyone, regardless of the
# core.autocrlf setting on the machine doing the clone.
* -text

# The .ps1 scripts are the entry point on Windows and are LF in the repository; both
# PowerShell 7 and Windows PowerShell read LF-terminated scripts without complaint.

# Generated artwork is text, but nothing should diff it by eye.
*.svg -text linguist-generated=true

# Keep the language statistics about the code rather than about its dependencies.
projects/**/wwwroot/lib/** linguist-vendored=true
docs/catalogue.json linguist-generated=true
tools/verification.tsv linguist-generated=true
